                <pb facs="0140" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.74/360: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-07-10T22:00:00-03:00">July 10, 1942—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 10—7:42 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1359. Embassy’s despatch 4338, March 6.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d94-f1"/> The
                    Minister of Interior<anchor n="44" xml:id="d94-f2"/> today addressed a note to
                    the Director General of Posts and Telegraphs<anchor n="45" xml:id="d94-f3"/>
                    quoting Resolution XL of the Rio conference and terminating as follows: <pb
                        facs="0141" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Consequently, it is necessary that Posts and Telegraphs adopt pertinent
                            measures for the purpose of complying with the provisions of said
                            resolution in such manner that the three points contained therein be
                            amply satisfied.</p>
                        <p>“The Director General will please advise if his agency finds itself in
                            condition to undertake the respective controls, and suggest measures
                            considered pertinent for such objective.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
